A||N||6||Cozmo||Fuel pressure question||||5||
Z||000000||Cozmo||05-12-2001||07:31 AM||||Just got a fuel pressure gauge.  When I hook it up to the test valve on the fuel rail of my 2.8 what should I see when....<P>A) Ignition on, engine not running?<BR>B) Engine running at idle?<P>When I pressurize the system, what kind of leakdown (if any) is acceptable?<BR>Thanks,<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><B>C02M0</B> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||05-12-2001||09:47 AM||||40.5 to 47 lbs PSI.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Vader||05-12-2001||10:41 AM||||You should get 40PSIG +/- 3PSI with the pump running and no vacuum at the FPR.  Leakage can be acceptable if there is still at least 15 PSIG 15 minutes after shut down.<P>------------------<BR>"<I>Make Me Bad</I>"||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cozmo||05-12-2001||11:02 AM||||I <B>assume</B> the "flow" is fuel pump to fuel filter to fuel pressure regulator to injectors and test valve.<BR><B>And</B> the FPR is supposed to be at about 45psi at ign. turnon and WOT then regulated downward depending on vacuum input...<BR>So am I smokin' that BAD s**t again or is this about right?<BR>Thanks,<BR>C02M0||||reg||14
Z||000004||Indiana_resto_guy||05-12-2001||10:19 PM||||Install your pressure gauge.<BR>Turn key to ON (no start)<BR>Check pressure if below above numbers, install new filter, start engine,shut off and recheck.<BR>If you still fail to get good pressure, bad pump.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cozmo||05-22-2001||08:32 AM||||Thanks for the T/S ideas, I tried them this weekend and here's what I've found...<BR>Turn on ign., fuel pressure GRADUALLY rises to about 20 psi.  Start/ run engine on starter fluid (I was careful, didn't drown it and wash all the oil off the cylinder walls) and the pressure never goes above 30. (engine runs fine, BTW). The pump relays and oil pressure sender contacts seem to work OK.<BR>OK... new filter first (easier to change than the pump <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">) no difference, same pressure readings.<BR>OK... belly up to the bar and do the pump and strainer.  Not as bad of a job as I anticipated, but no matter how careful I was gas got all over me and the floor  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">. Test results unchanged.<BR>OK...WTF???<P>I looked for plugged/ kinked lines, etc. checked the FPR vacuum feed and generally looked for something obvious. Nada...<BR>Is there a way I can safely test the pump directly, before the FPR?  I do have a spare fuel rail with FPR and injectors from a good car.  I hate to just start swapping parts but this problem is vexing me.  I just completed a top end rebuild and the car ran fantastic for about 80 miles before these symptoms cropped up.<BR>Any more ideas?<BR>Thanks again,<BR><B>C02M0</B>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Alex4mula||05-22-2001||08:42 AM||||Changed filter and pump? FPR was second easier. What about the FPR itself being bad? Change it with the spare one you said you have.||||reg||1
